# Pig Animations (single GLB)

All pig clips live in **`public/models/pig/pig.glb`**. Registry: `PIG_MODEL` + `PIG_CLIPS` in `src/constants/models.ts`.

## Clip names (inside pig.glb)

| Key | Clip name | Loop |
|-----|-----------|------|
| walkGun | Walk_Left_with_Gun | yes |
| run | Running | yes |
| aim | Archery_Aim_with_Lateral_Scan | yes |
| shoot | Archery_Shot_2 | no |
| deathAbdominal | Fall_Dead_from_Abdominal_Injury | no |
| deathShot | Shot_in_the_Back_and_Fall | no |

## Component pattern

- Use `PigAnimatedModel` — one `useGLTF` load, `SkeletonUtils.clone`, `useAnimations(animations, cloneRef)` on the **cloned mesh ref** (not the parent group).
- Crossfade with `fadeIn` / `fadeOut` when switching clips; do **not** remount the model per state.
- AK weapon is a separate `WeaponAk` attach — hidden during aim/shoot/run and when `weaponDropped`.

## Behavior → animation

| `Soldier.behavior` | Clip | Notes |
|--------------------|------|-------|
| biped | walkGun | patrol |
| aim | aim | drone in range, on cooldown |
| shoot | shoot | fires bullet, `shootTimer` counts down |
| flee | run | cowardly pigs or incoming munition; drops weapon |
| dead | deathAbdominal / deathShot | by `deathVariant` |

## AI (update-soldiers.ts)

- `cowardly` pigs (~45%) flee when drone within 14m and spot range 22m.
- Non-cowardly pigs aim/shoot instead of fleeing.
- Fleeing always sets `weaponDropped = true`.
